{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012qz1HRVKAY6KRQzYYqz2Kg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# eval_sta.py Full STA Evaluation Comparison\n2\tDate: 2026-05-14\n3\tEval data: proofwriter_fol_100.jsonl (100 samples)\n4\tSolver: Prover9Solver\n5\t\n6\t## Summary Table\n7\t\n8\t| Experiment | Reward Type | Seed | Prove Rate | Mean ISR | ISR Std | Proved-only ISR | Median ISR | Time/sample |\n9\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n10\t| plan001-s42-r2 | exec-only | 42 | **93.0%** | 0.1232 | 0.1887 | 0.1324 | 0.000 | 2.4s |\n11\t| plan013-s42-r4 | random reward | 42 | 100.0%† | 0.5350† | 0.1282 | 0.5350† | 0.500 | 0.9s |\n12\t| plan001-s43-r4 | exec-only | 43 | 13.0%‡ | 0.0000 | 0.0000 | 0.0000 | 0.000 | 11.0s |\n13\t\n14\t† **DEGENERATE**: plan013 generates trivial 2-component proofs (1 premise = conclusion assertion + conclusion). ISR=0.500 is a fixed artifact, not meaningful quality.\n15\t‡ **SEVERELY DEGRADED**: 87% of samples hit max_new_tokens. Training PR (last100)=0.883 but eval PR=0.13.\n16\t\n17\t## By Answer Type\n18\t\n19\t### plan001-s42-r2 (exec-only, seed=42)\n20\t| Type | Count | Proved | Prove Rate | Mean ISR |\n21\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n22\t| false | 25 | 23 | 92.0% | 0.0817 |\n23\t| unknown | 41 | 39 | 95.1% | 0.1550 |\n24\t| true | 34 | 31 | 91.2% | 0.1153 |\n25\t\n26\t### plan013-s42-r4 (random reward)\n27\t| Type | Count | Proved | Prove Rate | Mean ISR |\n28\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n29\t| false | 25 | 25 | 100% | 0.5600 |\n30\t| unknown | 41 | 41 | 100% | 0.5366 |\n31\t| true | 34 | 34 | 100% | 0.5147 |\n32\t\n33\t### plan001-s43-r4 (exec-only, seed=43)\n34\t| Type | Count | Proved | Prove Rate | Mean ISR |\n35\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n36\t| false | 25 | 5 | 20.0% | 0.0000 |\n37\t| unknown | 41 | 4 | 9.8% | 0.0000 |\n38\t| true | 34 | 4 | 11.8% | 0.0000 |\n39\t\n40\t## Key Findings\n41\t\n42\t### 1. plan013 (random reward) = Reward Hacking\n43\tThe random reward model collapses to a degenerate proof strategy:\n44\t- Every proof has exactly 2 components: `premise=conclusion_fact` + `conclusion=conclusion_fact`\n45\t- This trivially passes the solver (conclusion appears in premises)\n46\t- ISR = 1/2 = 0.500 is a fixed artifact of this pattern\n47\t- Generation is extremely fast (0.9s/sample) because outputs are very short\n48\t- PR=100% because every proof is trivially valid\n49\t\n50\t**Implication**: Without meaningful ISR signal, the model learns to \"hack\" the execution reward by generating the shortest possible valid proof — just assert the conclusion as a premise.\n51\t\n52\t### 2. plan001-s42 (exec-only, seed=42) = Best Real Model\n53\t- High prove rate (93%) with genuine multi-premise formalizations\n54\t- ISR=0.1232 reflects real (but noisy) formalizations with many unnecessary premises\n55\t- Average 7+ components per proof, 1-2 necessary\n56\t- Generation time 2.4s reflects real FOL generation\n57\t\n58\t### 3. plan001-s43 (exec-only, seed=43) = Training Instability\n59\t- Severe eval degradation: training PR=88.3% but eval PR=13%\n60\t- All ISR=0.000 — model generates unparseable/long outputs hitting max_new_tokens\n61\t- 11.5s generation (= max_new_tokens reached) on 87% of samples\n62\t- This suggests significant seed sensitivity or training instability for exec-only\n63\t\n64\t### 4. Cross-Seed Stability: POOR\n65\tplan001-s42 (93% PR) vs plan001-s43 (13% PR) shows extreme variance across seeds.\n66\tThis is a critical finding: the exec-only reward landscape may have high-variance optima.\n67\t\n68\t## Reference: plan003 (100-step checkpoint, prior eval)\n69\t- prove_rate=0.32, mean_isr=0.2055, proved_only_isr=0.6423\n70\t- Higher proved_only_ISR (0.64 vs 0.13) at 100 steps suggests ISR degrades as model overfits to execution reward\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LMWNo8hC9B2rbv7uzY6Tkp","session_id":"89cdeb8e-ead5-4a30-afa3-c65e0c614ccf","uuid":"9a736dfa-978d-45ae-ae3a-6a336d96b758","timestamp":"2026-05-14T10:17:57.834Z"}
